 "answer": "On a GPU with 32 GiB of VRAM, recent versions of Ollama default to a **32,768-token (32K) context length**. I believe Ollama sets the default by VRAM tier: under 24 GiB uses 4K, 24 to 48 GiB uses 32K, and 48 GiB or more uses 256K. Older releases used a much smaller default of 2,048 or 4,096 tokens, so the exact value depends on your Ollama version.\n\nYou can override the default with the `OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH` environment variable or the `num_ctx` option in an API request or Modelfile. Check your version's documentation or release notes to confirm the current defaults.",
